{"name":"Dixie","hex":"#cd8431","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dixie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Southern United States, especially the former Confederate States.","The southwestern corner of Utah."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dixie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dixie","blocks":[{"text":"Dixie, also known as Dixieland or Dixie's Land, is a nickname for all or part of the Southern United States. While there is no official definition of this region, or the extent of the area it covers, most definitions include the U.S. states below the Mason–Dixon line that seceded and composed the Confederate States of America, including all the Deep South. The term became popularized throughout the United States by songs that nostalgically referred to the American South."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Garrison%27s_Map_of_Dixie.jpg/330px-Garrison%27s_Map_of_Dixie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dixie","wikidata":"Q721983"},{"title":"Dixie (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dixie\", also known as \"Dixie's Land\", \"I Wish I Was in Dixie\", and by other titles, is a song first published in 1860 that is strongly associated with the Southern United States. It was not a folk song at its creation but has since entered the American folk vernacular. The song popularized the word Dixie in the American vocabulary as a nickname for the South."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/I_Wish_I_Was_In_Dixie%27s_Land%2C_1860.jpg/330px-I_Wish_I_Was_In_Dixie%27s_Land%2C_1860.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dixie_(song)","wikidata":"Q1231722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Bayou_Navigation_in_Dixie%2C_1863.jpg/500px-Bayou_Navigation_in_Dixie%2C_1863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Bayou_Navigation_in_Dixie%2C_1863.jpg/500px-Bayou_Navigation_in_Dixie%2C_1863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bayou Navigation in Dixie, engraving of a Louisiana steamboat, 1863","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABayou_Navigation_in_Dixie%2C_1863.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/DixBankNote.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/DixBankNote.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Ten-dollar note from Banque des citoyens de la Louisiane, 1860","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADixBankNote.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg/500px-Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg/1280px-Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg/500px-Gwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"C.D. Blake's I'se Gwine Back To Dixie and other similar songs included the usage of Dixie nostalgically. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGwine_Back_to_Dixie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Southern_United_States_by_Christopher_A._Cooper_and_H._Gibbs_Knotts.png/500px-Southern_United_States_by_Christopher_A._Cooper_and_H._Gibbs_Knotts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Southern_